## 2025/10/30-09.00

- **Recording**: <insert recording link>
- **Attendees**: Amparo Canaveras, Johnson, Evan, Prof. Ray
- **Topic**: Synthetic Data Pipeline, Architecture Review, Paper Structure & Action Planning
- **Summary**:
  The team discussed automation progress for wrong-parameter case generation, verification workflows, integration of synthetic data generation with SMO, paper structure refinement, prompt unification, GitHub consolidation, and upcoming experimental and writing tasks. Plans were set to finalize architectural diagrams, unify prompts, consolidate code/data repo, refine Section 3 of the paper, and produce preliminary fine-tuning results.
- **Discussion Points**:
  - **Automation & Dataset Update**
    - Evan automated CU/DU multi-parameter case generation, currently ~700–800 cases with varying success consistency:contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}
    - Error filtering by identifying folders without full result files (10 per case):contentReference[oaicite:1]{index=1}
    - Need to verify erroneous cases and finalize JSON path format for multiple wrong parameters:contentReference[oaicite:2]{index=2}
  - **Experiment Design**
    - Proposed experiment: train model on single-error cases and evaluate generalization to multi-error cases:contentReference[oaicite:3]{index=3}
  - **Architecture Clarification**
    - Discussion on what belongs inside SMO vs external components:contentReference[oaicite:4]{index=4}
    - Proposal to bundle synthetic data generation as an SMO RApp, SFT remains external due to compute constraints:contentReference[oaicite:5]{index=5}
    - Emphasis on clear expert-system architecture and interfaces (expert system ↔ SMO ↔ RAN):contentReference[oaicite:6]{index=6}
    - Multiple modules in expert system: config mutation agent, log collector, reasoning trace generator, SFT agent:contentReference[oaicite:7]{index=7}
  - **Paper Structure**
    - Section 2: clear system model (expert system, SMO, RAN):contentReference[oaicite:8]{index=8}
    - Section 3: describe expert system modules + include prompt design, pseudocode, GitHub refs:contentReference[oaicite:9]{index=9}
    - Repository + dataset exposure (GitHub + HF) planned:contentReference[oaicite:10]{index=10}
  - **Prompt Consolidation**
    - Need to unify Evan’s and Johnson’s prompts and test across models (Gemini, Cursor):contentReference[oaicite:11]{index=11}
  - **Follow-up Work**
    - GitHub cleanup and README build for reproducibility:contentReference[oaicite:12]{index=12}
    - Preliminary SFT results aimed for next week:contentReference[oaicite:13]{index=13}
- **Action Items**:
  - **Evan**
    - [ ] Verify error-producing cases and finalize filtering approach:contentReference[oaicite:14]{index=14}
    - [ ] Consolidate GitHub repo and add clear README + directory structure:contentReference[oaicite:15]{index=15}
    - [ ] Coordinate prompt unification + testing across models:contentReference[oaicite:16]{index=16}
  - **Johnson**
    - [ ] Refine system architecture diagram and align with expert-system modules:contentReference[oaicite:17]{index=17}
    - [ ] Test unified prompt variants and finalize prompt for the paper:contentReference[oaicite:18]{index=18}
    - [ ] Update paper Section 2 system model accordingly:contentReference[oaicite:19]{index=19}
  - **Amparo**
    - [ ] Provide example JSON format for multi-parameter wrong config paths:contentReference[oaicite:20]{index=20}
    - [ ] Draft Section 3 (expert system & synthetic data generation) with prompt details:contentReference[oaicite:21]{index=21}
    - [ ] Work on preliminary SFT results for the dataset:contentReference[oaicite:22]{index=22}
    - [ ] Share reference GitHub structure / framework example:contentReference[oaicite:23]{index=23}
  - **Prof. Ray**
    - [ ] Review updated architecture + Section 3 focus areas:contentReference[oaicite:24]{index=24}
    - [ ] Validate module boundaries and narrative for expert system vs SMO:contentReference[oaicite:25]{index=25}

